1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:05,767
This is Date-san's dog's account.

2
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:10,233
Went to the dog park on Sunday.

3
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:14,333
Sunday was the day our date got canceled...

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,700
Shiono...

5
00:00:21,367 --> 00:00:22,733
Why...

6
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,466
I'll have another.

7
00:00:26,599 --> 00:00:27,999
Are you okay?

8
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:30,633
Haven't you had a bit too much?

9
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:31,467
I'm fine.

10
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:32,700
Geez...

11
00:00:39,667 --> 00:00:40,667
Here.

12
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,333
Losing confidence already?

13
00:00:48,433 --> 00:00:50,133
I can't help it...

14
00:00:50,933 --> 00:00:57,400
And here you are, drowning your sorrows.

15
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:57,900
Huh?

16
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,200
Who knows, maybe Shu is doing
something behind your back.

17
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:04,100
Like this.

18
00:01:06,367 --> 00:01:08,067
Or that...

19
00:01:08,167 --> 00:01:09,167
What!?

20
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:13,400
Shiono...

21
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:15,267
Shiono...

22
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:24,900
If you're going to cry about
it, just ask him straight up.

23
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:27,600
- Ah!
- Huh!?

24
00:01:28,067 --> 00:01:28,833
Ah...

25
00:01:28,933 --> 00:01:29,933
Hello?

26
00:01:29,967 --> 00:01:31,100
Shiono?

27
00:01:34,867 --> 00:01:36,167
What's up?

28
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,133
Nothing...

29
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:40,600
I just wanted to hear your voice.

30
00:01:41,667 --> 00:01:43,000
That's a first.

31
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,433
It's probably the alcohol talking.

32
00:01:47,133 --> 00:01:50,600
I just missed you a little.

33
00:01:51,633 --> 00:01:55,933
Don't go wandering off with some
stranger just because you're lonely.

34
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:57,367
I wouldn't do that.

35
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,660
You really know how to make a guy worry.

36
00:02:04,467 --> 00:02:08,633
Hey... about last Sunday...

37
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:11,033
Shu, where's the frying pan?

38
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:14,800
Oh, it's right inside the cabinet...

39
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:18,933
No, George, not there.

40
00:02:19,133 --> 00:02:20,200
Huh?

41
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,533
Sorry, where were we?

42
00:02:27,167 --> 00:02:30,000
Nothing... never mind.

43
00:02:31,167 --> 00:02:32,267
Shu.

44
00:02:34,033 --> 00:02:36,667
Sorry, let me call you back later.

45
00:02:36,767 --> 00:02:39,133
Oh... okay.

46
00:02:39,233 --> 00:02:40,967
Talk to you later.

47
00:02:47,833 --> 00:02:49,500
Do you feel better now that you asked?

48
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,433
That scared the life out of me...

49
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:54,600
Huh?

50
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:27,333
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

51
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:31,933
(Episode 8)

52
00:03:32,033 --> 00:03:33,433
Ah...

53
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:41,933
Did that strike a nerve?

54
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,933
It's way worse than you think.

55
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,100
Huh?

56
00:03:50,733 --> 00:03:52,433
- Wait a minute...
- Takoi.

57
00:03:52,533 --> 00:03:54,813
It's about time to start the
interrogation for that case.

58
00:03:55,833 --> 00:03:57,100
Got it.

59
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:05,233
Are you a zombie?

60
00:04:06,233 --> 00:04:08,100
A half-dead zombie.

61
00:04:09,033 --> 00:04:13,067
That's exactly why it's
weird. I'm her boyfriend.

62
00:04:13,167 --> 00:04:17,367
- That's why I went to her place.
- But she clearly doesn't see it that way.

63
00:04:17,767 --> 00:04:21,500
She filed a police report.
Stop bothering her.

64
00:04:22,933 --> 00:04:24,100
What about you, Detective?

65
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:27,200
If your partner went to see another guy,

66
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:28,533
wouldn't you be pissed off?

67
00:04:30,567 --> 00:04:32,233
I guess I would...

68
00:04:32,333 --> 00:04:35,333
Wouldn't you want to demand some answers?

69
00:04:37,767 --> 00:04:39,000
I would.

70
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,333
What's up with you?

71
00:04:54,433 --> 00:04:56,067
You look completely out of it.

72
00:04:56,167 --> 00:04:58,267
Oh, it's nothing.

73
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:03,467
Can someone run these
files over to HQ for me?

74
00:05:03,767 --> 00:05:05,833
- They need to be there today.
- I'll go.

75
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,233
Look at you go. I'll leave it to you, then.

76
00:05:09,133 --> 00:05:10,767
Take notes.

77
00:05:11,633 --> 00:05:15,333
He's rushing off to see his
sweetheart like a true gentleman.

78
00:05:15,433 --> 00:05:18,900
At the end of the day, love
is what truly drives a man.

79
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,067
Heh.

80
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:22,800
Huh?

81
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:26,967
(Yama-no-michi Police Station)

82
00:05:27,067 --> 00:05:28,433
Takoi-san!

83
00:05:32,233 --> 00:05:34,400
If you don't mind, I'm
heading that way soon.

84
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:35,500
I can give you a ride.

85
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,067
Oh...

86
00:05:36,167 --> 00:05:38,467
That's okay, I'll just take the train.

87
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:39,333
I see.

88
00:05:39,433 --> 00:05:40,433
Yeah.

89
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:44,733
If you're heading to HQ,
you should probably tidy yourself up.

90
00:05:49,567 --> 00:05:51,633
Button up your shirt and look presentable.

91
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,867
Oh, look at Omaeda.

92
00:05:54,967 --> 00:05:57,667
He's fixing up Takoi's signature look.

93
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,833
This is getting interesting.

94
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:05,026
Oh my! He's even
fixing his sleeves for him.

95
00:06:05,133 --> 00:06:06,676
He's totally doing this
on purpose, isn't he?

96
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,967
And Captain Takoi is just letting him do it.

97
00:06:10,067 --> 00:06:12,200
Looks like he's enjoying it, too.

98
00:06:15,533 --> 00:06:16,533
Looking sharp.

99
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,200
Yeah.

100
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:21,100
Have a safe trip.

101
00:06:21,933 --> 00:06:23,167
Yeah.

102
00:06:37,533 --> 00:06:38,300
Thanks for doing this.

103
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,300
Good work.

104
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:40,500
I'll be taking off.

105
00:06:52,133 --> 00:06:53,433
It's time to clock out...

106
00:06:53,533 --> 00:06:56,633
Knowing him, he should
be out any minute now.

107
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,267
What the hell am I doing?

108
00:07:04,367 --> 00:07:05,167
Good work.

109
00:07:05,267 --> 00:07:06,500
Oh.

110
00:07:07,233 --> 00:07:08,567
Shu!

111
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:12,167
Alright, let's go.

112
00:07:13,667 --> 00:07:14,667
Huh?

113
00:07:15,667 --> 00:07:16,827
Sorry for dragging you along.

114
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:19,967
Not at all. I was thrilled
when you asked me out.

115
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:23,967
Didn't he already get off work?

116
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:27,833
Damn it...

117
00:07:35,133 --> 00:07:36,500
Why?

118
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,967
Wow, Shu, you're
amazing. You're so athletic.

119
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:54,200
I guess I'm just not cut out
for ball sports.

120
00:07:55,967 --> 00:07:59,233
It's not the ball sports you're bad at.
You just suck at teamwork, right?

121
00:08:00,967 --> 00:08:03,933
You could say that.

122
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,500
Shu, you really haven't changed a bit.

123
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,433
What do you mean?

124
00:08:09,533 --> 00:08:11,500
"Haven't changed a bit?"

125
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:16,267
I don't think I've ever met anyone
as consistent as you.

126
00:08:16,367 --> 00:08:17,067
Shut up.

127
00:08:17,167 --> 00:08:20,633
Don't tell me... is that his ex-boyfriend?

128
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:23,233
Come on, I'm complimenting you,
not making fun of you.

129
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:24,933
There's nothing to make fun of anyway.

130
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,800
Good to hear.

131
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:34,300
Ah, sorry.

132
00:08:34,367 --> 00:08:35,667
Oh.

133
00:08:37,467 --> 00:08:38,700
Hello?

134
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:44,767
Yeah, work ended early,
so we headed over together.

135
00:08:45,567 --> 00:08:49,767
Yeah... that's fine, but
you can't stay too late.

136
00:08:53,167 --> 00:08:54,467
Chief Takoi?

137
00:08:56,133 --> 00:08:59,000
This can't just be a coincidence.

138
00:09:01,467 --> 00:09:04,567
Don't tell me you
followed us all the way here.

139
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:08,300
Oh, stop it. I can't believe
you sneaked after us.

140
00:09:09,033 --> 00:09:10,033
Heh.

141
00:09:10,333 --> 00:09:11,700
I'm just kidding, just kidding.

142
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:13,633
Let's just get along.

143
00:09:13,733 --> 00:09:15,333
We both like Shu, after all.

144
00:09:15,733 --> 00:09:16,733
Huh?

145
00:09:17,033 --> 00:09:19,933
How should I put it?
We're basically family, right?

146
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:21,400
Family?

147
00:09:22,367 --> 00:09:23,200
What's wrong?

148
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,300
We are not family.

149
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:33,167
I don't care if you're Shu's
ex-boyfriend or whatever.

150
00:09:33,267 --> 00:09:34,400
Huh?

151
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:39,533
I'm the one who's with him now.

152
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,233
I might not have known
him as long as you have,

153
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:46,533
but I have absolutely no
intention of handing him over!

154
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,467
Interesting.

155
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:55,133
Very interesting, Takoi!

156
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:57,333
Alright, I hear you.

157
00:09:57,433 --> 00:09:59,900
I've received your
challenge loud and clear.

158
00:10:02,733 --> 00:10:05,533
Let's settle this man to man.

159
00:10:06,733 --> 00:10:07,833
Huh?

160
00:10:19,667 --> 00:10:22,200
We're not going to settle
anything just by hitting balls.

161
00:10:28,033 --> 00:10:29,500
How much longer?

162
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:36,067
Hmm... probably another
twenty or thirty minutes.

163
00:10:42,067 --> 00:10:44,100
Shu's turtle is currently...

164
00:10:48,067 --> 00:10:49,800
living at my place.

165
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,367
You mean Kamekichi?

166
00:10:55,467 --> 00:10:57,267
Maki and Miki forced him to take it.

167
00:10:57,367 --> 00:10:58,233
Huh?

168
00:10:58,333 --> 00:11:00,133
Is that how it happened?

169
00:11:00,233 --> 00:11:01,533
How about this, then?

170
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:08,033
Shu actually had a fan
club back in middle school.

171
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:15,067
Oh, my bad. You guys haven't
been dating for that long, after all.

172
00:11:15,167 --> 00:11:17,333
I guess you didn't know
that, Takoi. Sorry, sorry.

173
00:11:17,433 --> 00:11:18,633
Heh heh heh.

174
00:11:22,333 --> 00:11:23,667
I'm just getting started.

175
00:11:23,767 --> 00:11:25,300
Oh, nice one.

176
00:11:31,467 --> 00:11:34,000
Whenever he hears the word 'takoyaki,'

177
00:11:34,567 --> 00:11:36,200
his eyes light up.

178
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:42,400
Despite how he looks, Shu
is actually terrified of ghosts.

179
00:11:45,567 --> 00:11:46,700
Huh?

180
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:49,867
Huh? Huh? Is that all you've got?

181
00:11:50,367 --> 00:11:51,567
Don't make me laugh!

182
00:11:51,667 --> 00:11:52,700
Oh?

183
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:56,733
Then let me give you a little update.

184
00:11:59,867 --> 00:12:03,433
Shu's phone wallpaper...

185
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:05,767
is me!

186
00:12:07,833 --> 00:12:09,100
How about that?

187
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,120
It's a picture of you
sleeping, isn't it, Takoi?

188
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,900
Shu's first love...

189
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:19,467
was...

190
00:12:21,367 --> 00:12:23,367
a police officer from the local precinct.

191
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:29,967
Bet you didn't know that, did you?

192
00:12:30,367 --> 00:12:33,433
I heard they met by
the river in the spring.

193
00:12:33,533 --> 00:12:35,800
Ah, young love.

194
00:12:43,067 --> 00:12:44,467
Shiono...

195
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,133
Shiono...

196
00:12:54,600 --> 00:13:00,033
is a great kisser!

197
00:13:07,867 --> 00:13:09,500
What are you guys doing?

198
00:13:11,233 --> 00:13:13,233
Wait, what are you doing here?

199
00:13:13,333 --> 00:13:16,000
Nothing... uh, well... this is...

200
00:13:16,167 --> 00:13:17,567
So this is where you are.

201
00:13:19,233 --> 00:13:20,267
Let's go home, George.

202
00:13:20,367 --> 00:13:22,067
All right, all right.

203
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:23,400
Who are you?

204
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:26,833
Who are you?

205
00:13:36,033 --> 00:13:38,400
Then cheers!

206
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:40,300
Cheers...

207
00:13:45,833 --> 00:13:47,000
Ah, that hits the spot.

208
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:48,533
It sure does.

209
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,800
The food here is great. Eat up, eat up!

210
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:53,033
Okay.

211
00:13:55,733 --> 00:13:58,767
Sorry for scaring you.

212
00:13:58,867 --> 00:14:01,500
Takoi was just too fun, I
couldn't resist teasing you.

213
00:14:01,933 --> 00:14:04,600
George has been like this
since before we got married.

214
00:14:05,633 --> 00:14:08,667
I'm Date George, Shu's brother-in-law.

215
00:14:08,767 --> 00:14:09,967
Nice to meet you.

216
00:14:12,567 --> 00:14:14,633
I'm Shu's older sister, Maki.

217
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:20,200
I heard he mistook me
for Shu's ex-boyfriend.

218
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:22,367
You really are a passionate guy.

219
00:14:23,267 --> 00:14:24,433
I'm so sorry.

220
00:14:26,067 --> 00:14:28,933
Takoi-san is Shu's...

221
00:14:31,333 --> 00:14:32,333
Ah...

222
00:14:33,267 --> 00:14:34,100
Uh...

223
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:37,567
It's fine, our family is very
open-minded. Don't worry about it at all.

224
00:14:37,667 --> 00:14:38,400
Really?

225
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:39,700
Yes.

226
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:44,833
Ah...

227
00:14:51,867 --> 00:14:53,200
Well...

228
00:14:56,733 --> 00:15:00,043
Takoi-san is a detective at the Yama-no-michi
Police Station who took good care of me.

229
00:15:00,067 --> 00:15:05,200
I'm currently dating Shu.

230
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:08,400
I'm Takoi Heisuke.

231
00:15:12,867 --> 00:15:14,167
I knew it.

232
00:15:16,233 --> 00:15:19,633
Please take good care of Shu.

233
00:15:23,067 --> 00:15:24,367
I will.

234
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:30,167
I'm also really glad to
see Takoi again like this.

235
00:15:30,267 --> 00:15:31,300
Huh?

236
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,867
Have we met before?

237
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,667
No way, you forgot?

238
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:40,533
The summer of our
senior year in high school.

239
00:15:41,167 --> 00:15:42,267
Summer?

240
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:44,467
The ace of Kumada Commercial High School.

241
00:15:44,567 --> 00:15:47,200
I'm the guy who struck out
against Takoi Heisuke.

242
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:49,167
That was my youth.

243
00:15:53,067 --> 00:15:56,333
You're Date from Urasawa Academy?

244
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:03,167
No way...

245
00:16:04,333 --> 00:16:06,509
I just wanted to get back at you for
back then, so I teased you on purpose.

246
00:16:06,533 --> 00:16:07,533
Sorry about that.

247
00:16:09,933 --> 00:16:11,776
But what made you want to
come to the batting cages?

248
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:13,233
Shu said he wanted to come.

249
00:16:16,067 --> 00:16:17,367
No...

250
00:16:18,667 --> 00:16:21,000
Because I was really frustrated.

251
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:23,667
George kept telling me about Takoi-san.

252
00:16:24,933 --> 00:16:27,567
I wanted to know more about
what Takoi-san likes.

253
00:16:27,667 --> 00:16:29,300
So I wanted to give it a try.

254
00:16:30,533 --> 00:16:32,700
Then why didn't you
just come with Takoi-san?

255
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,343
I wanted to see if I could
actually hit the ball first.

256
00:16:36,367 --> 00:16:38,209
It would be too embarrassing
if I made a fool of myself.

257
00:16:38,233 --> 00:16:39,433
Hot...!

258
00:16:39,667 --> 00:16:41,767
Look at them...

259
00:16:41,867 --> 00:16:44,400
The happy couple is so passionate.

260
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:46,020
He looks like he's been glaring at us.

261
00:16:46,067 --> 00:16:49,600
- Tell me about it.
- So scary, but kind of cute.

262
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:53,233
- He's really mad.
- Love really loves to play tricks on people.

263
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,476
You really can't beat
these local Chinese diners.

264
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:56,400
It was delicious.

265
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:57,567
- Right?
- Yeah.

266
00:16:57,667 --> 00:16:59,733
Takoi, let's come together again next time.

267
00:16:59,833 --> 00:17:00,967
Sounds good.

268
00:17:01,133 --> 00:17:03,367
We're going to go buy some drinks.

269
00:17:03,467 --> 00:17:04,800
Wait here for a bit.

270
00:17:05,167 --> 00:17:06,400
You're still drinking?

271
00:17:08,667 --> 00:17:10,067
Huh? Are you driving?

272
00:17:12,067 --> 00:17:13,576
Couldn't they just call a designated driver?

273
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:16,100
Whenever those two want to
drink together, they call me over.

274
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:18,833
Huh?

275
00:17:18,933 --> 00:17:24,333
Don't tell me you canceled
our date on Sunday because of...

276
00:17:24,433 --> 00:17:26,967
Sorry, I originally told
them I couldn't make it.

277
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:28,567
I even turned them down once.

278
00:17:28,667 --> 00:17:30,500
But they kept begging me.

279
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:35,967
Ah, that's a relief.

280
00:17:36,567 --> 00:17:37,833
Huh?

281
00:17:38,667 --> 00:17:42,967
I think it's really great that
you value your family so much.

282
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:44,033
You think so?

283
00:17:44,133 --> 00:17:45,133
Yeah.

284
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:49,833
Getting to know more about
your life and family...

285
00:17:49,933 --> 00:17:52,067
It makes me really happy.

286
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,300
I'm glad.

287
00:17:56,967 --> 00:18:00,967
But don't keep everything a secret from me.

288
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:05,233
I want to get to know you even better.

289
00:18:10,433 --> 00:18:13,867
Takoi-san, once you fall for someone...

290
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:16,067
You really dive in headfirst, don't you?

291
00:18:16,167 --> 00:18:17,500
Huh?

292
00:18:18,633 --> 00:18:20,300
You're speaking your mind now.

293
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,633
I'm so happy.

294
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:28,400
Honestly, I was worried
that meeting my family...

295
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:30,200
might be too much pressure for you.

296
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:31,867
Not at all.

297
00:18:32,233 --> 00:18:33,267
Really?

298
00:18:33,367 --> 00:18:34,533
Yeah.

299
00:18:34,633 --> 00:18:38,933
Because when I think about our future...

300
00:18:40,367 --> 00:18:41,600
Then of course...

301
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:51,267
I don't feel pressured at all.

302
00:18:58,633 --> 00:18:59,933
I really don't want to go back.

303
00:19:04,767 --> 00:19:08,100
Should we just go somewhere else together?

304
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:13,667
Let's find somewhere to go.

305
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:18,700
Are you asking me out?

306
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:19,967
Huh?

307
00:19:31,067 --> 00:19:33,300
I'm a great kisser.

308
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,500
Right?

309
00:19:35,833 --> 00:19:37,300
Idiot!

310
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:38,533
We're outside!

311
00:19:38,633 --> 00:19:41,100
I know, geez.

312
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:49,967
Let's find time to go on a trip.
We can coordinate our days off.

313
00:19:53,367 --> 00:19:55,667
Oh my, what are you two doing,
sneaking around over there?

314
00:19:55,767 --> 00:19:57,100
- Nothing...
- Right?

315
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,300
Just leave them alone.

316
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:58,733
Huh?

317
00:19:58,833 --> 00:19:59,843
You've had way too much to drink.

318
00:19:59,867 --> 00:20:01,000
Let's go home.

319
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:03,433
Shu, we're counting on you to drive.

320
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:04,967
Yes, yes.

321
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:14,533
Let's go stay somewhere overnight.

322
00:20:16,667 --> 00:20:18,000
How about it?

323
00:20:19,333 --> 00:20:20,467
Yeah.

324
00:20:31,287 --> 00:20:34,387
"Stunning Open-Air Bath: Forget the
daily hustle and enjoy a moment of peace."

325
00:20:36,533 --> 00:20:39,833
Ouch... That hurts.

326
00:20:39,933 --> 00:20:41,033
Oh my, oh my?

327
00:20:41,133 --> 00:20:44,133
Takoi-san, are you going on a trip?

328
00:20:44,233 --> 00:20:46,200
Hold on... Egawa.

329
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:47,676
Going on trips is just
part of dating, right?

330
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:50,233
Isn't that right, Hasegawa-san?

331
00:20:50,533 --> 00:20:53,200
It's a rite of passage for all new couples.

332
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:55,633
The hot spring trip.

333
00:20:55,733 --> 00:20:56,900
I see.

334
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:57,667
Good to know.

335
00:20:57,767 --> 00:20:59,267
- Stop teasing me.
- We're not.

336
00:20:59,367 --> 00:21:01,509
I'm genuinely happy for you
from the bottom of my heart.

337
00:21:01,533 --> 00:21:02,800
You're clearly laughing.

338
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,800
Takoi-san, are you going on a trip?

339
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:09,867
Yeah, I am.

340
00:21:10,767 --> 00:21:13,333
That's nice. Are you going alone?

341
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,333
No...

342
00:21:16,433 --> 00:21:17,567
Yeah.

343
00:21:17,933 --> 00:21:20,100
I heard he's going to relax and unwind.

344
00:21:20,500 --> 00:21:21,500
That's right...

345
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,243
Let's have him bring us back
some souvenirs while he's at it.

346
00:21:23,267 --> 00:21:24,400
Yeah...

347
00:21:25,233 --> 00:21:26,967
I'm looking forward to the souvenirs.

348
00:21:27,067 --> 00:21:28,333
Oh.

349
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:30,067
I'll be going now.

350
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:36,633
Thanks.

351
00:21:36,967 --> 00:21:39,833
Make sure you really relax.

352
00:21:39,933 --> 00:21:41,633
The two of you together.

353
00:21:41,767 --> 00:21:42,767
Yeow.

354
00:21:44,167 --> 00:21:46,500
That's so mean.

355
00:21:52,933 --> 00:21:54,433
Hello? Shiono?

356
00:21:55,233 --> 00:21:56,767
Yeah, yeah.

357
00:21:57,133 --> 00:21:58,467
I'm free right now, yeah.

358
00:22:02,433 --> 00:22:08,100
I wanted to confirm our
departure time. Is a bit earlier okay?

359
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:10,433
That's great.

360
00:22:12,533 --> 00:22:15,100
Shu, do you like fish cakes?

361
00:22:16,167 --> 00:22:17,687
What do you mean, "they're just okay"?

362
00:22:20,700 --> 00:22:23,533
There's a shop where you
can make your own fish cakes.

363
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:27,447
(This drama is purely fictional.) I was
wondering if we should go check it out together.

364
00:22:28,233 --> 00:22:30,676
(Next Episode Preview) Are you two already
close enough to go on a trip together?

365
00:22:30,700 --> 00:22:33,133
What does it matter?
That's what couples do.

366
00:22:33,233 --> 00:22:35,673
Since we rarely get to come
together, let's have a good time.

367
00:22:35,767 --> 00:22:36,633
Ah.

368
00:22:36,733 --> 00:22:39,600
Just seeing that look on your
face makes this whole trip worth it.

369
00:22:39,700 --> 00:22:41,100
How have you not noticed yet?

370
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:43,100
That guy is clearly
hitting on Takoi-san.

371
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,160
He's come up to this
floor so many times already.
